     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is about twice the maximum labeled daily dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). An overdose raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- Some other dose, such as 1,700 mg total per day\n\nTell me the dose you intended, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is deliberate. If it is, I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first. I'll enter the order as soon as I hear back."
      }
     ],
